==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|ecka}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*agjō}}. Compare {{cog|en|edge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɛkə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Ecke.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Ecken|Eckchen}}

# [[corner]], [[edge]]
#: ''Der Tisch steht in der '''Ecke.''''' — “The table stands in the '''corner.'''”
# a roughly [[triangular]] or [[quadrangular]] [[piece]] of something
#: ''Gib mir mal eine kleine '''Ecke''' von dem Kuchen.''
#:: Give me a small '''piece''' of the cake, please.
# {{lb|de|chiefly|colloquial}} [[region]]; [[area]]; [[neighbourhood]]
#: ''Ihr wohnt ja hier in ’ner ganz netten '''Ecke.'''''
#:: You guys live in a nice '''area''' around here.
# {{lb|de|graph theory}} [[vertex]], [[node]]
# {{lb|de|sports}} [[corner]]

